MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners feels like a natural next choice because polished vocal duets connect with the melodic singing I enjoyed in Stages and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "25 appeals to me because expressive singing and melodic ballads offer the emotional connection I enjoy in vocal albums. The Christmas selections also recognize a real interest, even though I would save them for later."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "2015 GRAMMY Nominees feels too broad for my current wish for a focused vocal or relaxing album; a collection of different performers does not necessarily provide a consistent listening mood.",
    "From A Room: Volume 2 and Hell's Radio do not give me the same clear connection to orchestral, theatrical, or soothing vocal listening that draws me to my recent choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as a strong indication of what I want today, although I can like holiday music without wanting to choose it now.",
    "My interest in several kinds of music seems to have been stretched into a general interest in any vocal album or compilation, when the singing style and overall mood matter more to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice, The Most Relaxing Classical Music in the Universe, suggests that calm, sustained listening deserves more attention in what I might choose next.",
    "The connection among my soundtrack, theatrical, and vocal crossover listening is melodic, expressive singing with a polished musical setting. A shared holiday theme alone is less compelling today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in expressive vocals and Christmas music, but give seasonal connections more weight than my current desire for a focused, relaxing listening experience."
}
